{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VSmZ8FXGvdK42K5gA1itn1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# pace-bot\n2\t\n3\tA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\n4\tby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\n5\tprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\n6\tthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\n7\twhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\n8\tremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\n9\tits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n10\t\n11\tRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\n12\tmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n13\t`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\n14\tRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\n15\tprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\n16\tmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8cfd6da2-9c3f-42a5-8b3c-e74ced4f4226","uuid":"d9bf2505-6fa4-4289-9e50-c39c35208523","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:07:21.504Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-AZxpLJ/README.md","content":"# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n","numLines":17,"startLine":1,"totalLines":17}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VSmZ8FXGvdK42K5gA1itn1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
